WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.600
"You come up here."

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:12.680
We call it that fight mode. Eh, when you're in the middle of a fight you need to have all your adrenaline

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.800
on the maximum.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.700
"Shall we try?"

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.960
And when you have Wights attacking you from all sides, you're in that super maximum.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.180
To be able to, you've got to loosen up. You've gotta be ready for a fight.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.500
And it needs some screaming. It needs some hitting the axe.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.620
Even the extras are so into it. Ahhh. Oooohh. Ahhhh.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.540
"And she does arrive just in the nick of time. "

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.060
"Which is, you just have to. There's no other way that this scene could be written."

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.060
One of the main dramatic events of this is of course, the dragons coming to the rescue. And they're north of the wall

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:04.340
and so you get the direct, you know, explosion of fire against ice. Which is the central sort of motif of this

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.420
whole story saga.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:15.380
This is like a cutting torch, you know, going into a piece of ice. Imagine if you dump water into a blazing hot pot, it explodes.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.640
"Rolling and action."

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.340
I think back now and there was not a script when I spoke to David and Dan the first time about coming back to the season.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.300
But they told me the story.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.880
And then when they told me, you know, the details of the final scene.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.460
"Alright, everyone ready?"

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.040
And this was always the episode that was in some ways we're most excited about and also the most nervous about

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.320
because so much of it is dependent on those, you know, that final set piece actually working.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.040
"3,2,1 action"

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:06.200
The eyes of the White Walkers and the Wights have been such a prominent feature of the show and a lot of work

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:14.040
has gone into the specifics of how the eyes look and to see that hopefully iconic image at this point blown up to

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:20.380
the size of, you know, a beach ball. That seems like it was a crowd pleasingly oh shit moment.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.720
Hey everybody.This is my new Game of Thrones Q and A.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:30.100
But they also dropped this behind the scenes documentary for episode 6 right before I was getting ready to make it

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.300
So I just wanted to take some of the best bits of this and talk about it during this video in addition to the Q and A.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.080
So if you are finding me for the first time, we do Game of Thrones every week till Season 8 gets here.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.500
There'll be giveaway stuff at the end of the video.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.280
But don't you just love how crazy Tormund is on set.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.620
The actor that plays him, they're all great people, but the Brotherhood Without Banjos was probably one of the best

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.980
parts of all the behind the scenes Game of Thrones stuff this season.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.100
"You need to have all your adrenaline on the maximum."

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:03.380
So it's always cool to see Daenerys flying around and see how they do the dragons from a practical standpoint.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:07.200
And how they do the wights and these big battles. But really it's when they do these shots like this.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.060
Like just watching the actors try to get down all their sword swings the right way.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.980
But I know when the episode actually dropped it was very divisive for the things that it did not do.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.420
Namely kill one of these big name characters. Like if Jorah had died, that would have been really heartbreaking

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.140
in addition to the dragon.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.040
So Dan and Dave talk about how the entire episode turned around this scene here.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:33.160
So if this hadn't of worked, it would have just been an awful episode, but I feel like for all the dragon stuff, it actually did work out the way they wanted it to.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:39.640
So all those extra millions poured, literally poured as concrete into this area to make this lake ended up being

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.380
worth it.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.860
We can call Tormund explaining fights "Tormund-splaining"

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.940
So here we go, first question.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:49.340
GeeZEvil asked, "Qyburn needs a giant dragonglass arrow for his giant bow."

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:55.200
It's definitely a good idea. I feel like they could benefit from using the giant scorpion in combination with dragonglass.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.340
But there are a number of ways that he could go.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:02.980
The whole thing about the biggest deaths on the show, like you're talking about Cersei, Night King, Viserion.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:06.980
I think need to be especially meaningful for the characters that they're most meaningful to.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.860
So I think that the actual heartbreaking truth of it is that Daenerys will be forced to kill Viserion.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.320
She'll be forced to kill her child again.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:19.380
Think of it as another version of Cersei being faced with a choice to kill Joffrey.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.240
Like she said, "No matter how much of a monster he was, he was still my son."

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:29.680
So Daenerys still thinks of Viserion as her child. When she sees him again with a blue flame it'll break her heart all over again.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.020
Next question.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:36.160
Michael Ortiz asks, "What if the Night King is the 3rd dragon rider? The dragon has 3 heads."

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.280
Yeah there's been a lot of funny jokes about this going around since the season was over.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:45.380
I do think that that's the closest we'll get to the fulfillment of the prophecy. Unless you believe that Bran can

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.560
warg an undead dragon. That's really the crack pot theory that's gaining some steam.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:55.060
It's like what if Bran could warg the undead dragon and he becomes the 3rd head of the dragon?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.760
"You won't walk again, but you will fly."

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.580
Although in reality I think that quote was just about him warging the ravens and than flying around.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:03.700
Next one.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:09.980
Kyuketsu asks, "If they hadn't gone through the wall to get proof of the dead and lost a dragon, how would the Night King make it through the wall?"

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:14.900
Well. so this is actually what I think is going to happen in the books and it will involve the Horn of Winter.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:20.020
Remember after the Night King marked Bran and than it broke the magic seal on the Weirwood.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.780
People were like oh that's very clearly going to brake the magic seal on the wall. That's how they'll get through.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:30.760
But here's the thing, I feel like Dan and Dave as producers of a television show said that's not cinematic enough.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:37.400
Them just walking underneath the wall. We need to do something really big and grand. So even though George R. R. Martin told them the ending of

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:42.080
Game of Thrones, it's possible that they embellished the ice dragon part. Bringing the wall down.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.600
I think in the books it will be a little more subtle than that.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.720
And it will have something to do with the Horn of Winter.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:47.960
Next one.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:57.960
_sheisdeadjim_. Big Star Trek fan. "Do you think the dragons are going to die or will there be a new dynasty? I mean, would Dany need a new dragon if all her enemies are dead?"

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:05.020
Well, no, she wouldn't need a new dragon but I do think that the two dragons that are still alive will still be alive at the end of the season.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:12.040
Regardless of what happens to Jon Snow and Daenerys, I feel like there will be new dragon eggs. Like it's meant to be a Dream of Spring,

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:19.800
There's the idea that Daenerys might become pregnant again. She and her family have that deep connection to the dragons, so the idea that things would be born anew.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:26.700
Spring would come again. So that's just why I think there'll be more dragons in the future of this timeline even if they don't address it directly on the TV show.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.420
Like it depends on if there is a flash forward at the end of the finale episode.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:32.100
Next one.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:36.580
Xbitrate asks, "So if Summer is still around, could Bran warg him even if he's turned?"

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:43.420
Well that's actually a big question. It's just like Bran warging a dragon. George R. R. Martin's been asked that for a long time but never said definitively.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:49.100
I have speculated in the past that Bran's powers will grow as he learns more about them. I think given enough

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:53.800
time he could warg Summer and his powers flow from the Children of the Forest just like the Night King's.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:07:00.260
So if their powers come from the same place, than he could probably exert the same level of control over other beings.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:06.020
But I think the idea is, is that the Night King's consciousness sort of dominates all of the Wights that are risen.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:10.840
So Bran has to be more powerful than the Night King in order to break his control on someone.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.160
Next one.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.940
MM E asks, "Do you suppose we'll see Daenerys as a Wight?"

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.400
She's actually one of the few characters that I don't think is going to be turned into a Wight.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.760
Just because she's so tied to the dragons. I think Jon Snow and Daenerys are probably safe in that respect.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:26.980
There are a lot of theories about Jon Snow becoming the new Night King.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:32.260
But it depends on how you feel about the cycle of Ice and Fire. If the whole idea is to break the wheel,

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.880
